{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSca9p3mfqnQZHs9qH8V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (Order.kt:11) lacks status field\n- OrderController (OrderController.kt:22) provides POST /orders, GET /orders/{orderId}, GET /orders\n- OrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:10-26) uses in-memory ConcurrentHashMap storage\n- Shipment entity (Shipment.kt:9) already has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:10-26) lacks findByOrderId method\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt:26-43) creates shipments without order status checks\n- ApiError.kt (line 31-37) defines ErrorCode enum\n- ApiExceptions.kt (lines 18-24) defines ResourceNotFoundException and ConflictException\n- GlobalExceptionHandler.kt (line 14-28) centralizes exception-to-response conversion\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler serializes them\n- ResourceNotFoundException → 404, ConflictException → 409\n- ErrorCode enum is the single source of truth for error codes\n- Tests assert both status code and error envelope (code, message, fields)\n- In-memory repositories using ConcurrentHashMap\n\n**Affected files** — why each cannot be avoided:\n1. **Order.kt** — must add OrderStatus enum and status field, initialized to ACTIVE\n2. **ApiError.kt** — must add error codes for cancel scenarios (ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS, ORDER_CANCELLED_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT)\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — must add findByOrderId method to locate shipments for an order\n4. **OrderController.kt** — must add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — must validate order status before creating shipment\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — must add test cases for cancel endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n- If CONFIRMED shipment check is incomplete, a cancel with confirmed shipments could slip through\n- If retry handling is wrong, repeated cancel calls on already-cancelled orders could fail with 409 instead of succeeding\n- If ShipmentRepository doesn't query efficiently by orderId, the cancel operation becomes O(n) over all shipments\n- Serialization of new OrderStatus enum must be JSON-compatible (Spring auto-handles enum names)\n\n**Open questions:** None—the requirement fully specifies all cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add an OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and a status field to Order, defaulting to ACTIVE when created. The Order data class becomes: `Order(orderId, customerId, amount, currency, status)` with status defaulting to ACTIVE in the OrderController.create method.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Add two error codes to the ErrorCode enum:\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS` — thrown when cancel is blocked by confirmed shipments\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT` — thrown when creating a shipment for a cancelled order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `fun findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` that returns all shipments matching the orderId.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Add a `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Looks up the order, throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - Checks all shipments for this orderId\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException (409) immediately without changing state\n   - Otherwise, set order.status to CANCELLED, update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, save all, return the cancelled order\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, return it unchanged (idempotent)\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — In the create method, after checking for duplicate shipmentId, look up the order via a repository method and check if it's CANCELLED; if so, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add test cases covering:\n   - Cancel an active order with no shipments → returns 200 with order in CANCELLED status\n   - Cancel an active order with CREATED shipments → cancels them, returns 200\n   - Cancel an active order with a CONFIRMED shipment → returns 409, order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged\n   - Cancel an already-cancelled order → returns 200, no change (idempotent)\n   - Cancel a non-existent order → returns 404\n   - Add tests to ShipmentControllerTest for creating a shipment on a cancelled order → returns 409\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered using a service layer to encapsulate cancel logic, but the repository is simple in-memory storage and the OrderController already handles business logic inline (checking for duplicate orderId, throwing exceptions). Adding a service would be unrelated refactoring—the ticket says \"do not modify files outside the order and shipment features and the shared api package, except tests if required.\"\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Cancel ACTIVE order with no CONFIRMED shipments:**\n  1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n  2. OrderController.cancelOrder looks up order via repository.findById\n  3. Reads all shipments via shipmentRepository.findByOrderId\n  4. Checks if any have status CONFIRMED; none do\n  5. Updates order.status to CANCELLED, updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n  6. Saves updated order and shipments via repository.save\n  7. Returns 200 with the cancelled Order\n\n- **Cancel ACTIVE order with a CONFIRMED shipment:**\n  1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n  2. OrderController.cancelOrder looks up order, reads shipments\n  3. Detects CONFIRMED status\n  4. Throws ConflictException(ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS, ...)\n  5. GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, returns 409 with error body\n  6. Order and shipments remain unchanged\n\n- **Cancel already-CANCELLED order:**\n  1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n  2. OrderController.cancelOrder looks up order\n  3. Checks order.status is CANCELLED\n  4. Returns 200 with the order unchanged (idempotent)\n\n- **Create shipment for CANCELLED order:**\n  1. POST /shipments with orderId that is CANCELLED\n  2. ShipmentController.create checks for duplicate shipmentId\n  3. Looks up order via repository.findById\n  4. Detects order.status == CANCELLED\n  5. Throws ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT, ...)\n  6. GlobalExceptionHandler returns 409\n\n- **Create shipment for non-existent order:**\n  1. POST /shipments with orderId that doesn't exist\n  2. ShipmentController.create checks for duplicate shipmentId (passes)\n  3. Looks up order: not found, so repository.findById returns null\n  4. Skips the cancelled check (null order means it doesn't exist, existing behavior preserved)\n  5. Saves shipment as CREATED (existing behavior preserved)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest:**\n   - `cancel_active_order_with_no_shipments()` — creates order, cancels it, asserts 200 and status=CANCELLED\n   - `cancel_active_order_cancels_created_shipments()` — creates order, creates CREATED shipment, cancels order, asserts shipment is now CANCELLED\n   - `cancel_active_order_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409()` — creates order, creates shipment and manually sets it to CONFIRMED (via test setup), cancels, asserts 409 and order stays ACTIVE\n   - `cancel_cancelled_order_succeeds()` — creates order, cancels it, cancels again, asserts 200 (idempotent)\n   - `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404()` — cancel without creating order, asserts 404\n\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest:**\n   - `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409()` — creates order, cancels it, attempts to create shipment, asserts 409 with error code ORDER_CANCELLED_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nI'll now implement the changes in the order designed above."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1950,"cache_read_input_tokens":21706,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1950},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e86d816-595c-4ea4-8e13-265262b86d1a","uuid":"e0f06fb7-3cb8-4353-bab9-9bea8326e83b","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:37:09.211Z","request_id":"req_011CfSca9G3oQY3TcSstMzYg"}
