od. Necessary to locate all shipments for an order during cancel operation.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** — Added cancel endpoint and injected ShipmentRepository. The cancel endpoint implements the full business logic: order lookup, confirmed shipment check, idempotent handling, state transitions, and shipment cascade updates.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added order status check before creating shipment, injected OrderRepository. Necessary to block shipment creation on cancelled orders.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 5 new test methods and injected ShipmentRepository. Tests cover: cancel active order (no shipments), cancel with shipment cascade, cancel with confirmed shipment (409, no change), idempotent retry, and 404 for missing order.\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 new test method and injected OrderRepository. Test covers: rejecting shipment creation for cancelled order.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that transitions orders to CANCELLED status, cascades cancellation to CREATED shipments, rejects with 409 when CONFIRMED shipments exist, idempotently handles retries, and prevents shipment creation on cancelled orders\n\nChanged       Order.kt — added OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and status field\n              ApiError.kt — added error codes ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENTS and ORDER_CANCELLED_CANNOT_CREATE_SHIPMENT\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId(orderId) method\n              OrderController.kt — added cancel endpoint with full business logic and ShipmentRepository injection\n              ShipmentController.kt — added cancelled order validation and OrderRepository injection\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — added 5 new tests covering all cancel scenarios\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 1 new test for cancelled order validation\n\nTests         cance